course: dictionary
lesson: 12086
title: Clotted: lumps, cream and blood
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. «Clotted» is a good example. Look at the words around it, because they give you the clues.
explain: «The scone was served with jam and thick clotted cream.» Cream is food here, and a cream tea is a treat, so clotted cream must be a kind of cream. It is very thick and yellow.
explain: «The cut stopped bleeding once the blood had clotted.» A cut bleeds, and blood that has clotted has thickened into lumps, which helps to stop the bleeding. Here clotted is the past form of the verb clot.
explain: «Her hair was clotted with mud after the football match.» Mud stuck in lumps in the hair shows that clotted means thickened into lumps. Try the swap test: put «full of lumps» in place of clotted, and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Clotted means thickened into lumps, as in «clotted blood».
fact: Clotted cream is very thick yellow cream made by heating milk slowly.
fact: Clotted cream is famous in the south-west of England, and it is often eaten with scones and jam.
fact: As a verb, «clot» means to form clots, so «The blood clotted quickly» is in the past tense.
fact: When blood clots, it stops a cut from bleeding.
exercise: «The cook spread clotted cream on her warm scone.» What is clotted cream? | Cold water from a stream | A sort of cake with icing | A thin, watery drink | *Very thick yellow cream made by heating milk slowly
exercise: «The blood clotted quickly, so the cut soon stopped bleeding.» What does clotted mean here? | Went very cold | Spread across the floor | Was washed away | *Formed clots, thickening into lumps
exercise: «His hair was clotted with mud after the match.» What does clotted mean in this sentence? | Clean and shiny | Brushed neatly | *Stuck together in lumps | Dried into flakes like snow
test: Which word in «Her hair was clotted with mud» tells you the mud is sticking in lumps? | match | hair | *clotted | mud
test: Ben says clotted cream is a type of cake. Is he right? | No, it is a thin drink | Yes, it is a sort of cake | *No, it is a very thick yellow cream | Yes, it is a sweet biscuit
exam: What does clotted mean in «clotted blood»? | Moving very fast | *Thickened into lumps | Bright red and wet | Hot and steaming
